  "text": "There are 60 minutes in an hour.\n\nTo calculate the volume of the cylinder with a radius of 4 cm and a height of 10 cm:\n\nThe formula for the volume of a cylinder is:\n$$V = \\pi r^2 h$$\n\nWhere:\n*   $r$ is the radius (4 cm)\n*   $h$ is the height (10 cm)\n\nSubstituting the values:\n$$V = \\pi \\times (4)^2 \\times 10$$\n$$V = \\pi \\times 16 \\times 10$$\n$$V = 160\\pi$$\n\nUsing $\\pi \\approx 3.14159$:\n$$V \\approx 160 \\times 3.14159$$\n$$V \\approx 502.65$$\n\nThe volume is approximately **502.65 cubic centimeters**."
